@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
!include _uml-style.puml
title A successful session — UML sequence
hide footbox
participant "caller" as Caller
participant "<color:#FFFFFF>native front\n<color:#FFFFFF>(runner inside)" as Front #1E4F78
participant "<color:#FFFFFF>policy worker" as Worker #1E4F78
participant "managed process" as Managed
database "result channel\n(temporary files)" as Channel #FFF1CF

Caller -> Front : start-session: kind and prompt
Front -> Front : Admit inputs and policy path
== Selection ==
create Worker
Front -> Worker : Start in empty private directory
Worker -> Worker : Change to /
Worker --> Front : Identity; front checks the match
Front -> Worker : Send policy request (no session-result context)
Worker -> Worker : Import owner policy; select
Worker --> Front : Policy response on private socket
Front -> Front : Judge response; confirm worker reap;\nremove worker's private directory
destroy Worker
Front -> Front : Resolve selected executable
== Launch and publication ==
create Channel
Front -> Channel : Allocate fresh result channel
create Managed
Front -> Managed : Launch in its own process group;\npass session-result context
Managed -[#135E50]> Channel : Publish opaque result via end-session
note over Managed, Channel
  First complete publication wins.
  Publication does not wait for cleanup.
end note
== Cleanup and delivery ==
Front -> Managed : Stop the managed process's group\n(grace and escalation if needed)
Front -> Front : Confirm direct-child reap; recover terminal\nif lent; confirm process-group absence
destroy Managed
Front -> Channel : Validate and read published result
Channel -[#135E50]-> Front : Exact opaque value
Front -> Channel : Remove result channel's temporary directory
destroy Channel
Front -> Front : Settle cancellation and cleanup outcomes
Front -[#135E50]> Caller : Write and flush opaque result; exit 0

legend bottom
  Read downwards: message order, not elapsed time. Dashed verticals: lifelines.
  Solid arrows: actions; dashed arrows: replies. Bent arrows: work within a participant.
  An X ends the pictured lifetime after reap or removal, not at process exit.
  Blue: Ravel processes. Grey: external participants. Gold cylinder: temporary files.
  Green arrows carry the opaque result. Labelled bars group stages, not processes.
  Successful unconfined path only; terminal recovery applies only if lent.
  Publication precedes cleanup; only the last arrow delivers the result to the caller.
endlegend
@enduml
